<title>UK: McCarthy &amp; Stone sale will eliminate debt.</title>
<headline>McCarthy &amp; Stone sale will eliminate debt.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>British property group McCarthy &amp; Stone Plc said on Tuesday it had sold its freehold reversionary interests and its leasehold flat interests to Fairhold Homes Ltd for around 10.7 million stg.</p>
<p>It said in a statement the interests had a combined current income stream of 950,000 stg and that the sale would generate a profit of around 1.5 million for McCarthy.</p>
<p>The proceeds will eliminate McCarthy &amp; Stone's bank borrowings and leave the firm with a net cash balance.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
